  "notes": "Source: Holmes Community College official 2025-2026 Bulletin (Amendment Number II Part A) 'Occupational Therapy Assistant Technology, AAS', hand-transcribed 2026-10-02 from the official amendment PDF. The map lists no inline prerequisites unless stated below. An AAS Degree is earned after the five consecutive semesters below. Students must maintain at least a 75 in each course to progress. Anatomy & Physiology I & II (BIO 2514/2524) are required prerequisites for the program (modeled as external_prereqs). *MAT 1233 Intermediate Algebra and a natural science with lab (7 hrs. total) may be substituted for MAT 1313 College Algebra, making the first semester 18-22 hrs. Program notes: students progress through five consecutive semesters; all graduation and fieldwork requirements must be completed within 9 months after the didactic portion. Graduates are eligible to take the National Certification Exam for Occupational Therapy Assistant. Enrollment in a minimum of 15 hours each semester is recommended for state aid, institutional scholarships, and the tuition break.",
